  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (3 of 3).\n\nThe new tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js`. They cover every example in the spec, version ordering, prerelease handling, and invalid inputs, which return `false` without throwing.\n\nThe spec leaves a few cases open, so I made these calls:\n- **Prerelease identifiers:** numeric ones with leading zeros are invalid, so `1.2.3-01` returns `false`. This follows standard semver.\n- **Wildcard followed by a number:** a range like `1.x.3` is invalid and returns `false`.\n- **Fully wildcard bounds:** `>*` and `<*` match nothing. `>=*`, `<=*` and `=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n- **Hyphen ranges:** a hyphen range must be the whole comparator set. Mixing it with other comparators, as in `>=1 1.2 - 2`, is invalid.\n- **Large numbers:** version numbers are compared as `BigInt`, so very large numbers compare correctly.",
